{
  "_about": [
    "Field semantics (#526): what a decoded field IS, as data. Two decisions, in order:",
    "1. scaffolding — frame plumbing that must never be plotted: a field whose LAST",
    "   path segment is in `scaffolding_leaves`, or whose path contains a segment in",
    "   `scaffolding_segments`. Segments are matched whole: `ax25_header` is framing,",
    "   `ax25_frame` is the container most decoders put the payload in (767 of the",
    "   fleet's 1315 fields sit under it), so it is NOT a marker.",
    "2. measure — a field whose last two segments carry a `state_leaves` token is a",
    "   state; otherwise the first entry of `measures` whose `match` regex hits the",
    "   lowercase field wins; `unit` and `range` describe what a plausible value looks",
    "   like. Order matters: `temperature` sits before `current` so `..._temp_i` is a",
    "   temperature.",
    "`overrides` correct the guess per decoder, by trailing path (1..n segments): a",
    "value of a measure name, \"scaffolding\" or \"unknown\". A wrong guess is a",
    "one-line edit here, not new SQL. Step 3 (#526) worked the unknown list decoder",
    "by decoder: 244 names, of which the ones a .ksy makes unambiguous are mapped",
    "below and the rest (analog1..5, compass_misc, dosimeter channels) stay unknown",
    "on purpose — a guess is worse than a gap."
  ],
